# Serie D (EN): il Sole nei 12 segni, un discorso unico per segno che cita le tradizioni.
PLANET='Sun'
COVER_SUB='What your Sun feels like in each sign.'
S=[
('Aries','Fire · cardinal','Exaltation','The Sun is exalted in Aries: this is the equinox, where the days begin to grow longer than the nights, and you feel that victory as a drive to start, to lead, to be first. It is the pure affirmation of the self, impulse before reflection, with courage, speed and a temper that flares and cools fast. Spiritually it is the soul taking its first step into form, a new cycle opened by a single act of will. The shadow is impatience and a need to win every argument. The lesson: let the fire build something.'),
('Taurus','Earth · fixed','Venus’s sign','Taurus is a fixed sign ruled by Venus, so the Sun stops rushing and takes root. You want what you can touch: good food, music, land, steady income, people who stay. Patience is a real strength here, and so is stubbornness; once you decide, you rarely turn back. It is the sign of the body, the senses and endurance, and in its deeper meaning of light: desire slowly refined into understanding. The shadow is possessiveness and fear of change. The lesson: what you value should serve you, not own you.'),
('Gemini','Air · mutable','Mercury’s sign','Gemini is a double sign ruled by Mercury, and the Sun here is always two things at once: speaker and listener, student and teacher. You collect words, people and information, and you fit into any room. Relationship and exchange are at the heart of this sign. Its duality is also inner: the soul and the personality, both speaking, not yet sure which is which. The shadow is scattering and a restless mind that never lands. The lesson: depth comes from staying with one thing a little longer.'),
('Cancer','Water · cardinal','The Moon’s sign','Cancer is a tropical sign: the Sun turns at the summer solstice, and the sign belongs to the Moon. The Sun here becomes receptive and protective. Your identity grows from home, family, memory and mood, and you sense what others need before they say it. An ancient image calls Cancer the gate through which souls enter life; it is the sign of mass life and of building a form to live in. The shadow is clinging and withdrawal. The lesson: a shell is for protection, not for hiding.'),
('Leo','Fire · fixed','The Sun’s own house','Leo belongs to the Sun, as Cancer belongs to the Moon: the two lights each have their house. Here the Sun shines without effort. You are warm, proud and generous, with a need to create and to be seen. It is the creative self and natural authority; the sign of the heart, just as the Sun is the heart of the solar system. Its deeper meaning is an individual finding full self-awareness, so that it can later serve the group. The shadow is vanity and a wound when ignored. The lesson: a true king lights the room for others.'),
('Virgo','Earth · mutable','Mercury’s sign','Virgo, ruled by Mercury, brings the Sun down to the field: harvest, craft, order, health. You see the detail others miss, and you show love by being useful. Analysis, service and discernment are its tools. Its old image is the Mother and the Child, spirit hidden in matter, and the sign is the slow work of giving an ideal a real form. The shadow is perfectionism, worry and a harsh inner critic. The lesson: being useful does not require being flawless.'),
('Libra','Air · cardinal','Fall','Libra is the Sun’s fall, opposite its exaltation. It is also an equinoctial sign, where night begins to overtake day. The sign belongs to Venus and defines itself through others, so the Sun feels less sure of its own centre. You are fair, charming and a born diplomat, driven by association and harmony. Its deeper meaning is a balance between two forces and the mind that must choose between them. The shadow is indecision and pleasing everyone. The lesson: peace that costs you yourself is not peace.'),
('Scorpio','Water · fixed','Mars’s sign','Scorpio is a fixed water sign ruled by Mars, and the Sun goes below the surface. You feel strongly, show little and see through pretence. Crisis, secrets, desire and loss are your territory. It is the sign of transformation, and of testing and initiation, where the warrior must cross his own illusions to be free. The shadow is jealousy, control and a long memory for wounds. The lesson: every ending you survive teaches you how to begin again.'),
('Sagittarius','Fire · mutable','Jupiter’s sign','Sagittarius is ruled by Jupiter, and the Sun here looks to the horizon. You are frank, optimistic and hungry for freedom, travel, philosophy and meaning. You inspire others with sheer enthusiasm. It is expansion and a search for truth. Its image is the archer who aims straight at one goal, and when he reaches it, sees another beyond. The shadow is exaggeration, impatience with detail and preaching what you only just learned. The lesson: faith is stronger when it can tolerate a doubt.'),
('Capricorn','Earth · cardinal','Where the Sun turns','Capricorn is the winter solstice, where the Sun turns and the light starts to return. It belongs to Saturn. You are patient, responsible and willing to work for years toward a goal, often serious young and lighter with age. Concentration and ambition are its strengths. An ancient tradition calls it the gate of the gods, and its image is the mountain goat climbing toward the will to manifest. The shadow is coldness and fear of failing. The lesson: authority is stronger when it is human.'),
('Aquarius','Air · fixed','Opposite the Sun’s house','Aquarius is Saturn’s other house, directly opposite Leo, and the Sun feels slightly out of place. You are independent, inventive and committed to ideas bigger than yourself. Friends and causes matter more to you than applause. Modern astrology adds Uranus, the planet of emancipation and the unexpected. Its image is the water carrier, pouring out the water of life for others. The shadow is detachment and rebellion for its own sake. The lesson: belonging to a group does not mean dissolving in it.'),
('Pisces','Water · mutable','Jupiter’s sign','Pisces is a double water sign, given to Jupiter and later to Neptune. The Sun dissolves into the sea: you are intuitive, compassionate and moved by music, art and other people’s pain. Boundaries are thin, so you absorb the moods around you. It is the sign of the saviour and of faith and the unconscious, and it governs our present age. The shadow is escape, confusion and martyrdom. The lesson: kindness needs a shore to stand on.'),
]
